  "result": "Payment terms feature complete! All 181 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **TERMS_INVALID error** to src/errors.js\n2. **getLastDayOfMonth()** helper in src/dates.js to calculate the last day of any month (handling leap years and all month lengths)\n3. **Terms support in createInvoice()**: \n   - Accepts optional `terms` parameter: 'NET14', 'NET30' (default), or 'EOM'\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` based on the payment terms\n   - NET14: due 14 days after issue date\n   - NET30: due 30 days after issue date\n   - EOM: due on last day of the issue date's month\n   - Returns TERMS_INVALID error for unknown terms\n4. **20 new tests** covering:\n   - Default and explicit NET14/NET30/EOM terms\n   - Due date calculations for various scenarios (leap years, month boundaries)\n   - Terms preservation through addLine, removeLine, and issueInvoice\n   - Error handling for invalid terms\n5. **7 new tests** for getLastDayOfMonth() covering all month types and edge cases\n\nTerms and dueDate are properly preserved when invoices go through addLine, removeLine, and issueInvoice operations.",
